findings.detail:
Declarations, `src/routes/library/+page.svelte:181-183`:
```
let bulkCheckoutWorkId = $state('');
let bulkCheckoutEditionId = $state('');
let bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers = $state<Set<string>>(new Set());
```
All writes found by grep across the whole file:
- `bulkCheckoutWorkId`: `:775` (auto-select effect, `bulkCheckoutWorkId = works[0].id`), `:1089` (select `onchange`).
- `bulkCheckoutEditionId`: `:782` (reset effect keyed on work-id change), `:1096` (select `onchange`).
- `bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers`: `:788` (reset effect keyed on edition-id change), `:1066` (cleared after a successful submit in `handleBulkCheckout`), `:1120-1123` (checkbox toggle, builds a new `Set` and assigns it).
None of these seven sites reference a collective switch.

The route-load `reset` callback, quoted in full, `:313-319`:
```
reset: () => {
    expandedWorks = new Set();
    expandedEditions = new Set();
    editionsByWork = new Map();
    copiesByEdition = new Map();
    repertoireByWorkId = new Map();
},
```
It is passed to `createRouteLoadMachine` (`:307-322`), which per the comment at `:303-306` fires this unconditionally on every (re)selection. It clears five caches; `bulkCheckoutWorkId`, `bulkCheckoutEditionId`, `bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers` are absent. Confirms the issue's claim verbatim.

Quoted in full, `:779-789`:
```
// #74 — reset edition when work selection changes
$effect(() => {
    void bulkCheckoutWorkId;
    bulkCheckoutEditionId = '';
});

// #74 — reset checked state when edition selection changes
$effect(() => {
    void bulkCheckoutEditionId;
    bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers = new Set();
});
```
Each keys on exactly one reactive read (`void <var>` establishes the Svelte dependency with no other use). A `$effect` re-runs only when a tracked value actually *changes*. On a collective switch, nothing writes `bulkCheckoutWorkId` (confirmed in finding 1 — `reset()` doesn't touch it, and the only other writer is the user-driven select `onchange` at `:1089`), so its value is byte-identical before and after the switch; the first effect never re-fires, so `bulkCheckoutEditionId` is never reassigned; its value is likewise unchanged, so the second effect never re-fires either. A separate, unrelated `$effect` at `:772-777` (`if (works.length === 1) bulkCheckoutWorkId = works[0].id`) auto-selects a work when there is exactly one — this is not a reset and is not one of the two the issue names, but it does interact with any switch-time clear (see finding 6).

Quoted in full, `:1039-1072`:
```
async function handleBulkCheckout(): Promise<void> {
    bulkCheckoutError = '';
    const current = selected;
    if (!current) return;
    const token = getToken();
    if (!token) return;
    const libraryId = $libraryEntityIdStore;
    if (!libraryId) return;
    if (!bulkCheckoutEditionId || bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers.size === 0) return;
    const cfg = { db: current.db, token };
    const activeLendings = lendings.filter((l) => l.returnedAt === '');
    try {
        const result = await bulkCheckout(cfg, libraryId, {
            editionId: bulkCheckoutEditionId,
            memberIds: [...bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers],
            assignedAt: new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10),
            ...(bulkCheckoutDueDate ? { assignedUntil: bulkCheckoutDueDate } : {})
        }, activeLendings);
        if (result.failed.length > 0) {
            bulkCheckoutError = `${result.failed.length} checkout(s) failed`;
        }
        const lendingList = await listLendings(cfg);
        const activeMemberIds = lendingList.filter((l) => l.returnedAt === '').map((l) => l.memberId);
        const names = await resolveBorrowerNames(cfg, activeMemberIds);
        lendings = lendingList;
        borrowerNames = names;
        bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers = new Set();
        bulkCheckoutDueDate = '';
    } catch (e) {
        console.error('library: bulk checkout failed', e);
        bulkCheckoutError = e instanceof Error ? e.message : 'Bulk checkout failed';
    }
}
```
Reads: `selected` (current collective), token, `$libraryEntityIdStore`, `bulkCheckoutEditionId`, `bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers`, `bulkCheckoutDueDate`, `lendings`. Guards present: non-null `current`, `token`, `libraryId`, non-empty `bulkCheckoutEditionId`, non-empty `bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers`. None of these five checks compares the ids against the *current* collective — there is no `isCurrent()`-style generation guard and no comparison of `bulkCheckoutWorkId`/`bulkCheckoutEditionId` against anything scoped to `current`.

**Confirmed per the PO's added finding**: `memberIds: [...bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers]` (`:1053`) spreads the raw `Set<string>` of member ids straight into the POST body passed to `bulkCheckout(cfg, libraryId, {...}, activeLendings)`. `bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers` is declared as `Set<string>` holding `member.memberId` values (checkbox handler `:1118-1123`), so a foreign collective's member ids are what would be posted, not merely displayed.

The derived value, `:806-810`:
```
let bulkCheckoutEditionAvailability = $derived(
    bulkCheckoutEditionId
        ? deriveEditionAvailability(bulkCheckoutEditionId, allCopies, lendings)
        : { available: 0, total: 0 }
);
```
`deriveEditionAvailability`, `src/lib/library/libraryData.ts:364-374` (quoted in full):
```
export function deriveEditionAvailability(
    editionId: string,
    copies: Copy[],
    lendings: Lending[]
): { available: number; total: number } {
    const editionCopies = copies.filter((c) => c.editionId === editionId);
    const available = editionCopies.filter(
        (c) => deriveCopyAvailability(c.id, lendings).status === 'available'
    ).length;
    return { available, total: editionCopies.length };
}
```
It is a pure filter with no notion of "unknown id" as a distinct case — an id matching zero copies and an id that legitimately has zero copies produce the identical `{available:0,total:0}`. This is exactly the issue's point: nothing marks the zero as meaning "foreign," so any future change to the function's unknown-id handling (a default, a fallback lookup) would silently remove the block. The button's disabled expression, `:1135`: `disabled={bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers.size === 0 || bulkCheckoutCheckedMembers.size > bulkCheckoutEditionAvailability.available}` — with `available` pinned at 0 for a foreign id, any non-empty selection (`size > 0`) is disabled by the second clause, and an empty selection is disabled by the first; the button is unreachable for every value of `checkedMembers.size`. `handleBulkCheckout` itself also independently returns early on an empty `checkedMembers` (finding 3), so even a hypothetical DOM-bypassing click can't submit an empty set either.

**Total vs. partial — traced the async race, found no live window.** I checked whether the arithmetic could ever be evaluated against *stale* `allCopies`/`allMembers` (i.e., before they're refreshed for the new collective) while the panel is visible/clickable. `allEditions`/`allCopies`/`allMembers` are populated only inside the `librarianGen` effect (`:915-955`): `resetLibrarian()` (`:922`) synchronously sets `librarianStore` to `'loading'` the instant `selected` changes; the entire bulk-checkout section is gated behind `{#if $librarianStore === 'librarian'}` (`:1079`, closing `:1141`), so it is unrendered for the whole reload. `librarianStore.set(result.state)` (`:953`), the only write that can flip it back to `'librarian'`, sits *after* the `await Promise.all([listAllEditions, listAllCopies, listActiveMembers])` and the `allEditions=/allCopies=/allMembers=` assignments (`:932-940`) in the same async continuation — there is no code path that sets `librarianStore` to `'librarian'` before those three arrays are refreshed for the new collective. So by construction, every render in which the button is visible and enabled has already-fresh `allCopies` for the currently selected collective; a `bulkCheckoutEditionId` left over from a *different* collective will not match any entry in that fresh array (Entu ids are not shared across collectives — [unverified], relies on Entu's id-scoping, not re-confirmed this turn), so `available` is reliably 0 whenever a foreign id is retained. I did not find a reachable state at HEAD where a stale cross-collective selection gets past this arithmetic and posts. **This is [speculative] insofar as it depends on Svelte 5's effect-flush ordering never exposing an intermediate frame with a stale-but-enabled panel, which I did not instrument/observe directly, only inferred from the source's sequential-await structure** — but nothing in the code offers an alternate path to `librarianStore==='librarian'` that skips the refresh. My conclusion: **the bug is latent, not currently live** — it matches the issue's own framing ("the button never enables"; "invisible on screen") rather than contradicting it, but the PO's done-when is still correct to insist on this because the zero-coincidence is fragile by construction, not because it is currently failing to hold.
